# IMPL-0002 demo env. Copy to demo/.env (gitignored) and edit.
#
# `make demo-up` reads demo/.env via compose. Variables fall into three
# groups, one per phase. Default values are safe for local play; rotate
# them if you publish the stack anywhere.
#
# ┌──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────┐
# │ Group                │ Used by                              │ Required when?   │
# ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────┤
# │ 1. demo-api          │ demo-api validates /api/bearer       │ always           │
# │ 2. MCP boundary      │ demo-mcp accepts on /mcp             │ always           │
# │ 3. OIDC (Phase 5)    │ demo-idp + demo-api oauth2flow       │ make demo-up-oidc│
# └──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────┘
#
# Every "Phase N" reference below points at the same phase in
# docs/impl/0002-docker-compose-demo-and-integration-harness.md.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. demo-api bearer auth (Phase 1a — always set)
#
# The token /api/bearer/{,/{id}} expects on the upstream side. Both
# demo-api (validates) and demo-mcp (forwards via the proxy bearer)
# read it. Tools that hit the bearer tree fail with `upstream 401`
# without it.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEMO_BEARER_TOKEN=demo-secret-please-change

# Optional: split the proxy's outbound bearer from the API's inbound
# expectation. When unset, demo-mcp uses DEMO_BEARER_TOKEN (round-trip).
# Set to a different string to verify the failure path (mismatched
# tokens → upstream 401 on /api/bearer/*).
# MCP_DEMO_API_TOKEN=

# slog level for demo-api: debug | info | warn | error
DEMO_LOG_LEVEL=info

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. MCP boundary auth (Phase 1b — always set for `make demo-up`)
#
# The inspector must send `Authorization: Bearer <MCP_BOUNDARY_TOKEN>`
# (UI-paste, not env) before /mcp will accept the connection. Distinct
# from DEMO_BEARER_TOKEN so the two perimeters can rotate
# independently. demo-mcp reads this from env and matches it against
# whatever the inspector pastes.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MCP_BOUNDARY_TOKEN=mcp-boundary-secret-please-change

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. OIDC flow (Phase 5 — only set when running `make demo-up-oidc`)
#
# The default `make demo-up` does NOT use any of these. They wire the
# Phase 5 OIDC variant: demo-idp issues RS256 JWTs; demo-mcp validates
# inspector JWTs against its JWKS; demo-mcp forwards a separate
# service-account JWT to /api/oauth2flow. Leave commented for the
# bearer demo — the empty default is harmless but the comments below
# make the intent obvious.
#
# To activate the OIDC flow:
#   1) Switch HCL: `make demo-up-oidc` (regenerates from mcpgen-oidc.hcl).
#   2) Mint a service-account JWT: `make demo-mint-service-token`.
#   3) Uncomment + paste the value below as MCP_OAUTH2_SERVICE_TOKEN.
#   4) `make demo-rebuild`.
#   5) Mint a user JWT: `make demo-mint-user-token`. Paste into the
#      inspector's headers panel as `Authorization: Bearer <user-jwt>`.
#
# Issuer + audience defaults match the compose service's internal DNS;
# override only if you publish demo-idp behind a reverse proxy.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDP_ISSUER=http://demo-idp:5556
# IDP_AUDIENCE=mcp-demo-api
# MCP_OAUTH2_SERVICE_TOKEN=
